"Ran it — exit 0, `app.ini` created in `/workspace/project`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Size | 61 bytes |\n| Lines | 5 |\n| `\\r\\n` line endings | 5 of 5 |\n\n`od -c` confirms a literal `\\r` before every `\\n`, so the file is genuinely Windows-style CRLF, not LF with the escape chars dumped raw:\n\n```\nn a m e = d e m o \\r \\n h o s t = l o c a l h o s t \\r \\n ...\n```\n\n`printf` interprets `\\r\\n` in the format string, so this worked as intended. One note: if shellcheck-style portability matters, `printf '%s\\r\\n' \"name=demo\" \"host=localhost\" ...` is safer, since `\\r` isn't in POSIX's required escape set for all `printf` implementations — but bash/dash both handle it fine."